    1	# FOCUS-1: Connes-Consani-Moscovici operator scaling -- results
    2	
    3	**Status:** CLOSED via Equivalence (mode E). Chain A is not a polylog architecture.
    4	
    5	**Date:** 2026-04-26 (Session 50)
    6	
    7	**Script:** `connes_operator_scaling.py` (single file, ~250 lines)
    8	
    9	## Question
    10	
    11	Does the rank-one perturbation of the scaling operator from CCM (arXiv:2511.22755)
    12	admit a polylog architecture? Specifically, define
    13	`K_accurate(B) := largest K such that |mu_K^op(B) - gamma_K^true| < 0.5`.
    14	
    15	If `K_accurate(B) = polylog(B)` Chain A is real polylog (huge).
    16	If `K_accurate(B) = O(B)` or below, Chain A closes via Equivalence.
    17	
    18	## Operator construction (proxy, NOT exact CCM reproduction)
    19	
    20	Discretize the scaling operator `D = -i d/du` on `L^2([-L, L])` (`u = log t`,
    21	`L = log(lambda) = (1/2) log(x_cutoff)`, `x_cutoff = 10^4`) on Fourier basis
    22	`phi_n(u) = exp(i pi n u/L)/sqrt(2L)`, `n = -N..N` with `N = 1200` (matrix size 2401).
    23	`D` becomes diagonal with `d_n = pi n / L`.
    24	
    25	Add a self-adjoint rank-one perturbation `V = c |v><v|` where `v` encodes primes
    26	`p <= P_max(B)` plus their prime powers via the von Mangoldt weighting:
    27	
    28	- **`delta_comb` variant:**  v(u) = sum_{p^k <= e^L}  (log p)/sqrt(p^k) * delta(u - log p^k),
    29	  Fourier-projected onto the basis. (Selected by tuning -- best matched-error.)
    30	- **`psi_step` variant:**  v(u) = sum_{p^k}  (log p)/sqrt(p^k) * 1[u in [log p^k, L]].
    ... (134 more lines)
