    1	"""
    2	Proposal 25: Liouville-Parity Triangulation
    3	
    4	Identity (corrected during this experiment): with
    5	    L(x) = sum_{n<=x} lambda(n)              (Liouville summatory)
    6	    C_3(x) = #{n <= x : Omega(n) is odd and >= 3}
    7	the count #{n <= x : Omega(n) odd} = (x - L(x))/2 since Omega(1)=0 is even,
    8	so
    9	    pi(x) = (x - L(x))/2 - C_3(x)
    10	and in particular
    11	    pi(x) mod 2 == ((x - L(x))/2 - C_3(x)) mod 2.
    12	
    13	The original proposal mis-identified C_3 with (Q(x)-1).  This experiment:
    14	  (a) confirms the corrected identity,
    15	  (b) probes whether C_3(x) admits a polylog parity oracle of its own,
    16	  (c) tests truncated-L_K reconstructions.
    17	
    18	Run:  python3 proposal25_liouville_parity_check.py
    19	"""
    20	
    21	import time
    22	from sympy import factorint, primepi
    23	
    24	
    25	def Omega(n: int) -> int:
    26	    """Total number of prime factors of n with multiplicity."""
