    7	
    8	## Top-line finding
    9	
    10	The Liouville-identity attack on `pi(x) mod 2`,
    11	
    12	    pi(x) = (x - L(x))/2 - C_3(x)             (E2.2 / S46),
    13	
    14	is now closed at the **structural-pseudorandomness** level (in addition to
    15	the identity-bottleneck closure of S46).  Each component of the
    16	decomposition — `A(x) mod 2 = (x - L(x))/2 mod 2` and `C_3(x) mod 2` —
    17	is independently pseudorandom under all standard measures, and the two
    18	are statistically independent (MI ≈ 2 × 10⁻⁵ bits).
    19	
    20	Two new pseudorandomness measures are added to
    21	`novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md`: #25 `A(x) mod 2`, #26 `C_3(x) mod 2`.
    22	
    23	## New algebraic observation (free identity)
    24	
    25	`L(x) mod 2 = x mod 2` is trivially true for every x:
    26	
    27	> L(x) = sum_{n=1..x} lambda(n) with lambda(n) ∈ {-1, +1}, so L(x) mod 2 =
    28	> sum of parities = x mod 2.
    29	
    30	Verified bit-exact for all 2 000 000 sampled x.
